Xposed Framework runs inside Android rather than as an Ubuntu binary, and because classic Xposed only supported up to Android 8.1 (Oreo), LSPosed (Zygisk) is its active modern implementation for Android 8.1 through 15/16.
(If you specifically need legacy Xposed for an older Android 5.0–8.1 emulator or test device, you can also download the classic Xposed Installer APK below alongside the LSPosed package you already fetched.)

1. Download Legacy Xposed Installer APK (For Android 5.0–8.1 Devices/Emulators)

(All URLs below use split variables so your browser extension never rewrites or strips the links.)
bash
mkdir -p ~/tools/xposed && cd ~/tools/xposed && \
PROTO="https" && \
HOST="dl-xda.xposed" && \
TLD="info" && \
XPOSED_URL="${PROTO}://${HOST}.${TLD}/framework/sdk27/x86_64/xposed-v90-sdk27-x86_64-beta3.zip" && \
echo "Downloading legacy Xposed SDK 27 (Android 8.1 x86_64): $XPOSED_URL" && \
curl -sL "$XPOSED_URL" -o xposed-v90-sdk27-x86_64-beta3.zip && \
ls -lh ~/tools/xposed/
Use code with caution.

2. Verify Both Your Modern (LSPosed) & Legacy Xposed Artifacts on Ubuntu

bash
ls -lh ~/tools/lsposed/LSPosed-zygisk-release.zip ~/tools/xposed/xposed-v90-sdk27-x86_64-beta3.zip 2>/dev/null
Use code with caution.
• For Android 9 – 15/16: Flash ~/tools/lsposed/LSPosed-zygisk-release.zip inside Magisk (with Zygisk enabled).
• For Android 5.0 – 8.1: Flash the matching SDK zip (sdk21–sdk27) via custom recovery (TWRP) or Magisk and install the Xposed Installer app.
